    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: e3f3517e6ef70ddadf773bd2389cfdcf813ea862 -->\nReviewer: wopr pool job review-4333, GPT-6 (Codex), mkinney; did not write or refresh this PR.\n\nClean. No blocking findings. The PR merges cleanly with main.\n\nI read the full diff and issue #3560. I used upstream main's current AGENTS.md.\nThe quick mapper keeps its selection rule. The heavy mapper uses that rule and keeps the documented fallback.\nThe decision file records the trade-off. The body has `Process change: yes`. The PR does not change PROCESS_VERSION.\n\n## Local results\n\nWorktree: `.claude/worktrees/review-4333`.\nTrial merge: `510400f63da48857668241a035808283c0f4c369`.\nBase: `eafe6aec6ec74ad34c5e0643648e2d97791ef149`.\nThe first parent is the reviewed PR head.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: PASS. One step, zero failures. All xtask targets pass, including 364 unit tests and the three new Gate map pins.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: PASS. Six steps, zero failures. All 11 light twins pass.\n  - Release build: PASS.\n  - `motion light: lib`: 7 passed.\n  - `motion light: adaptive_troch_island`: 1 passed.\n  - `motion light: adaptive_troch_neck`: 1 passed.\n  - `motion light: adaptive_troch_parallel`: 1 passed.\n  - `app light: pocket_pass_start`: 1 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: zero steps reached. Full heavy lanes were not run.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: fails at unchanged `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`. The same command fails identically on bare upstream main at the base above. This is not a PR blocker.\n\n```text\nerror: this `if` guard returns a bool literal and is followed by another\n  --> xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67:5\n```\n\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings -A clippy::needless_bool`: PASS on the trial merge.\n\n## Extra suites run\n\nNone beyond quick and light. The diff changes only xtask and a decision file.\nIt changes no fixtures, importers, posts, operations, motion code, catalog entries, recorded programs or UI code.\nNo goldens moved. Catalog and kernel suites do not apply.\n\n## Safety and mutations\n\nThis is not a safety-tier change. It changes no posted G-code, geometry, collision checks, gouge checks or stock simulation.\nI did not repeat the author's mutations. No mutation rerun is required for this tier.\n\n## Requested before merge\n\nNone.\n\nOwnership record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4333#issuecomment-7217652322\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
